 "note": {
  "status": "draft",
  "text": "In algebra a letter stands for a number we do not know yet, for example x.\nWriting words as an expression:\n• 3 more than x: x + 3   • 5 less than x: x − 5 (not 5 − x)\n• twice x, or 2 times x: 2x   • x times y: xy\n• x divided by 4: x ÷ 4, also written x/4   • the square of x: x² (x × x)\nRules for writing: put the number before the letter (3x, not x3), leave out the × sign (3 × x = 3x), and write x, not 1x.\nStories: Ashu has x francs and spends 200 francs: she has x − 200 francs left. Five books at x francs each cost 5x francs.",
  "checks": []
 },
 "worked_example": {
  "status": "draft",
  "vars": {
   "n": 4,
   "c": 150
  },
  "problem": "Mbah buys {n} exercise books at x francs each and a pen at {c} francs. Write an expression for the total cost.",
  "steps": [
   "{n} books at x francs each cost {n} × x = {n}x francs.",
   "Add the pen: {n}x + {c}."
  ],
  "answer": "The total cost is {n}x + {c} francs.",
  "checks": [
   "n * 2 + c == 158"
  ]
 },
